Third-party components keep their own licenses:

- three.js (MIT License), loaded from cdnjs at runtime.
- Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, licensed under the Open Database
  License (ODbL) 1.0: https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/
  Any redistribution of the extracted OpenStreetMap data must follow the
  ODbL, including its attribution and share-alike terms.
- Elevation tiles: Mapzen terrarium terrain tiles on AWS Open Data.
  See the dataset's terms before reusing them.

- Kenney Car Kit 3.1 GLB review candidates in `media/vehicles/traffic/`:
  original models by Kenney, Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal,
  https://kenney.nl/assets/car-kit ; unchanged copy from the public
  https://github.com/Hidencod/tge-assets mirror on 2026-11-13.

- Volvo 240 experiment reference images only (not game textures):
  `experiments/volvo240/references/{side,front,rear}_review.png` are resized
  copies of photographs by Vauxford, CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ . Source file pages:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1990_Volvo_240_GL_2.3_Side.jpg
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1990_Volvo_240_GL_2.3_Front.jpg
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1990_Volvo_240_GL_2.3_Rear.jpg
  The side comparison crops/flips/resizes that photo; its photograph portion
  retains this licence. No endorsement is implied.
- `experiments/volvo240/references/three_quarter_review.png`: resized photograph
  by OSX, public domain. Source:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1990_Volvo_240_GL_sedan_(2015-06-03)_01.jpg
- Experiment uses external Blender Modeler helpers by calebrisc (MIT):
  https://github.com/calebrisc/blender-modeler . Its source is not vendored into
  this repository; its licence remains in its external checkout. The vehicle
  geometry is newly authored and contains no imported third-party 3D mesh.
- Vehicle preview libraries vendored in `media/vehicles/vendor/`: Three.js r128
  and its matching GLTFLoader, MIT License. Full licence text is included as
  `media/vehicles/vendor/THREE-LICENSE.txt`. These are the same versions previously
  loaded by the preview from CDNs; local copies avoid extra third-party requests.

- Saab 900 experiment reference PNGs in `experiments/saab900/references/`:
  photographs by Alexander Migl, CC BY-SA 4.0,
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/ . Resized PNG conversions;
  no photo textures are included in the original procedural model. Sources:
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saab_900_(first_generation)_three-door_hatchback_Turbo_DSC_2936.jpg
  https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saab_900_(first_generation)_three-door_hatchback_Turbo_DSC_2938.jpg

Saab silhouette review reference excerpt:
experiments/saab900/silhouette/reference.png is a small crop from the Danish
Saab 900/900i brochure, copyright Saab-Scania AB 1985, sourced at
https://motorarkiv.dk/brochurer/SAAB_900_og_900i_1985.pdf . It is included only
for technical comparison and criticism, not licensed as a reusable game asset.
No rights to the original brochure are claimed. The generated vehicle itself
and original pipeline code do not incorporate the image as textures or geometry.

XC70 reference images (experiments/xc70p2/references), technical study only:
front.jpg, front-2.jpg: Bull-Doser, public-domain dedication, source links in
experiments/xc70p2/references.md; front-detail.jpg is a resized crop.
rear-three-quarter.jpg: Ethan Llamas, CC BY-SA 4.0, resized.
police.jpg: Fifo, CC BY-SA 2.5, unchanged.
police-new.jpg: Per Enström / Plrk, CC BY-SA 4.0, unchanged.
side.png / rear.png and spec.pdf: Volvo UK XC70 Technical Specification April
2003, copyright Volvo. Technical-comparison excerpts, no game-asset licence
claimed. Author/source/licence URLs and modifications: experiments/xc70p2/references.md.
Generated body, original livery raster and POLIS lettering contain no reference
photograph pixels. No endorsement by Volvo or the Swedish Police is implied.

